# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -2 in a three-player game, with an empty slot before the target (CR 608.2b): Bot1 chooses nothing
# for Bot2, whose Ornithopter is a candidate, and Bot3's Ornithopter for Bot3's slot; the targets are [none, Ornithopter]. In response
# Bot3 Lightning Bolts its own Ornithopter, which dies. Its only target is now illegal, so the ability does nothing: Bot2's
# Ornithopter - not a target - is not returned either, and stays on the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
The Theorist, Jace Beleren
Island x4
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x6
Island x12

[Bot3 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x4
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot3.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Activate(Ability: For each opponent)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot3.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot3.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot3.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
Bot3.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.The Theorist, Jace Beleren.Counters.Loyalty = 1
Stack.Count = 0
